      {
        "id": 159162,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-09T13:02:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Maynes32\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/c5a1d2/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Maynes32:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hmm. A fair point. I edited my post while you were replying. I would think that when you have a situation like that in my edit - two semi-proximate appearances in the same book, with different costumes, that should evade the artist/cross issues … er … issue. ;)&nbsp;BLM</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I'll give a quick example of a instance where costumes are not consistent.</p>\n<p>PW Argent Adept. At some points he dresses in his PW costume as seen in Cap Cosmics deck. But we have instances of Argent fighting the Aeon Men in his normal costume which must happen really late in the story.</p>",
